            <ArticleTitle>Subacute total occlusion of the left main coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>411</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Total occlusion of left main coronary artery (LMCA) is a rare manifestation of coronary atherosclerotic disease. The exceptionality of this illness is due to its high mortality rate before any treatment. We report a patient with subacute total occlusion of the LMCA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
